        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Globalization is the **compression of time and space** through intensification of cross-border flows of capital, goods, information, people, and culture. The digital revolution has accelerated every dimension of globalization while creating new asymmetries — a \"network society\" (Castells) in which power flows through informational networks, and a \"surveillance capitalism\" (Zuboff) in which human behavioral data becomes the raw material of a new economic logic."
    },
